  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Consider points $A(-5,0)$, $B(5,0)$, and $C(3,4)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that the points all lie on the circle $x^2+y^2=25$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$OA=OB=OC=5$, so all three points lie on the circle $x^2+y^2=25$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}OA&=\\sqrt{(-5)^2+0^2}=5\\\\OB&=\\sqrt{5^2+0^2}=5\\\\OC&=\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5\\end{align*}$$\nEach point is 5 from the origin, so all three lie on the circle with equation $x^2+y^2=25$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $AC\\perp BC$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$m_{AC}=\\frac12$ and $m_{BC}=-2$. These are negative reciprocals, so $AC\\perp BC$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AC}&=\\frac{4-0}{3-(-5)}=\\frac12\\\\m_{BC}&=\\frac{4-0}{3-5}=-2\\\\m_{AC}m_{BC}&=\\frac12(-2)=-1\\end{align*}$$\nThe gradients are negative reciprocals, so $AC\\perp BC$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      }
    ]
  },
